course: dictionary
lesson: 12693
title: Divert: changing the way
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To divert something means to make it change direction or go a different way. «The road was closed, so the buses had to divert through the village.» The buses did not stop. They took a different route, and that is what divert means.
explain: Divert can also mean to take someone's attention away from something. «The magician waved his left hand to divert the audience's attention from his right hand.» Divert is a verb, so it changes its form: divert, diverts, diverted, diverting.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. Words like road, traffic, flight or route often show that divert means change direction. Words like attention show that it means pull away from something. Then swap in your meaning, such as "sent a different way", and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: «Divert» is a verb: divert, diverts, diverted, diverting.
fact: «Divert» means to make something change direction or go a different way, as in «divert traffic».
fact: «Divert» can mean to take someone's attention away from something, as in «divert attention».
fact: «Divert» can also mean to use money, time or supplies for a different purpose, as in «divert funds».
exercise: «The road was closed, so the buses were diverted through the village.» What does diverted mean here? | Stopped for ever | *Sent along a different way | Made much faster | Painted bright red
exercise: «The magician waved his hand to divert the audience's attention.» What does divert attention mean? | Ask everyone to sit down | Give extra attention to a dog | *Take attention away from something
exercise: The council will «divert funds» from the old park to fix the roads. What does divert funds mean? | *Use the money for a different purpose | Count the coins | Throw the money into the river | Lock the money in a box
test: The storm meant the flight was «diverted» to another airport. What happened to the flight? | It was cancelled and never flew | *It was sent to a different airport | It landed at the same airport as planned | It flew slower than usual
test: Which word shows that the bus changed its route? | Parked | *Diverted | Stopped | Waved
exam: «The sign said Diversion, so we turned left to avoid the closed bridge.» What does diversion mean in this sentence? | A loud noise | A type of bridge | *A different route to follow | A picnic spot
